\f0\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Removing 
\f1\b Bunker Ultimatum
\f0\b0  actually helps. It leaves the final Johnny\'96Chip scene as the first time Chip has enough evidence, and enough fear, to try to 
\f1\b stop the project outright
\f0\b0  rather than merely warn about it.\
I\'92d make the final run of Project Kebab roughly:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Two-disc elliptical rail becomes routine.
\f0\b0  Johnny proves he can move the harnesses, alter geometry and compensate phase while keeping the two fields well behaved. This establishes the machine before the stolen discs appear.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Five-disc debut: Missing Socks.
\f0\b0  The three off-book discs appear. All five run. The reader has Rotherhithe hanging over the experiment, probably refreshed by the quake-trance diversion. Instead of catastrophe they get a remarkably clean communication: 
\f2\i Missing Socks
\f0\i0 . Johnny is vindicated in his own mind.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Post\'96Missing Socks escalation.
\f0\b0  Johnny starts exploring what improved coherence buys him. More speed. More aggressive movement around the ellipse. More simultaneous control of the 26 possible groupings. The local/remote earthquake pair belongs well here. It is disturbing evidence, but Johnny can still explain it as an understood side-effect of a functioning system rather than runaway instability.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Johnny decides to push towards 30,000 rpm.
\f0\b0  This is what brings Chip running. Importantly, rpm alone isn't what terrifies him. Chip has seen high rotational speeds before. The frightening thing is 
\f1\b 30,000 rpm combined with five discs whose relative geometry is continuously changing while Johnny's controls deliberately maintain coherence
\f0\b0 .\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Chip tries the ordinary engineering objections first.
\f0\b0  Bearings, containment, field strength, Rotherhithe, remote effects. Johnny has answers. The machine is instrumented. Missing Socks worked. The phase compensator works. They can predict at least some remote effects. Every modification Chip warned against has so far made the apparatus behave 
\f2\i better
\f0\i0 .\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	6	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Sarah forces Chip to say what he has been withholding.
\f0\b0  This is where closed resonance finally enters the novel. During the terminal moments of the Goa event, Fridge Force recorded something they could never fit into a normal sequence of cause and effect: the resonant state appeared back through the generating array in a way paired with a generator state that had not yet occurred. At the same time, the distinction between the Goa apparatus and the supposedly remote locus temporarily disappeared. Fridge Force called the condition 
\f1\b closed resonance
\f0\b0  because that was less embarrassing than admitting their equations no longer offered a useful before and after.\uc0\u8232 They could never reproduce it.\u8232 Then comes the vital detail: 
\f1\b the Ark couldn't change its geometry.
\f0\b0 \uc0\u8232 Three platter centres were fixed. The discs could change speed and phase, but the spatial relationship between them was essentially locked. Goa happened to pass through the closed-resonance condition and immediately passed out of it again.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	7	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Sarah looks at Johnny's rail.
\f0\b0  This should do more work than another paragraph of Chip exposition. Five articulated harnesses are moving around the ellipse. Their axes can change. Their relative positions can change. Johnny's control system is continually adjusting phase to 
\f1\b keep the fields coherent while all that happens
\f0\b0 .\uc0\u8232 Johnny's answer is perfectly rational:\u8232 That is the improvement.\u8232 Chip's answer is the core of the whole arc:\u8232 That is the problem.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\strokec3 The specific Fridge Force warning Chip has finally remembered\'97or has gone back and found\'97was that a system capable of 
\f1\b changing relative geometry while preserving coherence might remain inside the closed-resonance condition instead of merely crossing it
\f0\b0 .\
That gives Johnny a much stronger position than generic hubris. He can say, in substance: 
\f2\i Goa was an uncontrolled accident. This is controlled. When the geometry changes, my system compensates.
\f0\i0 \
And Chip can answer: 
\f2\i Yes. It compensates.
\f0\i0 \
That word should become horrible.\
The machine isn't merely capable of stumbling onto the dangerous configuration. Johnny has built a system designed to 
\f1\b follow a desired coherent state as the configuration changes
\f0\b0 .\
At that point Chip wants it stopped. Completely.\
Sarah is the authority who can stop it, so the scene needs to become hers briefly. She should be deciding between two men who both have evidence:\
Johnny has 
\f1\b Missing Socks
\f0\b0 .\
Chip has 
\f1\b Goa
\f0\b0 .\
Johnny has repeatable control.\
Chip has one unrepeated anomaly buried in an old Fridge Force appendix.\
Johnny's machine has done what it was supposed to do every time it has improved.\
Chip is telling Sarah that this success is precisely what now makes it dangerous.\
That is a genuine decision rather than Sarah merely believing whichever scientist sounds most frightened.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f3 \strokec3 <$Scr_H::3>
\f1\b\fs28 How the universe ends\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f3\b0\fs24 \strokec3 <!$Scr_H::3>
\f0 I wouldn't have Johnny deliberately disregard Sarah ordering a shutdown and mash a button. That would throw away the argument and turn him stupid at the last second.\
The machine should already be running during the confrontation, below the intended maximum, while Johnny is demonstrating or preparing the next stage. Sarah finally sides with Chip\'97or is just about to\'97and tells Johnny to bring it down.\
Then something changes.\
Perhaps Johnny says the phase error has suddenly fallen.\
Chip looks.\
The compensator is no longer working hard to maintain coherence.\
It barely has to work at all.\
The moving geometry has found a state in which each adjustment makes the next required adjustment smaller.\
Johnny sees extraordinary stability.\
Chip recognises something else.\
The system has found 
\f1\b closed resonance
\f0\b0 .\
And the truly nasty part is that shutting down may no longer have the ordinary meaning everyone thinks it does. Once the apparatus is part of a wave-relational state in which generator, remote locus and the state being generated are no longer separable in time, cutting the motors now may already be included in whatever state has closed around them.\
You don't need a long cosmological spectacle.\
Chip understands first.\
Johnny perhaps understands one beat later.\
Sarah may understand only that both men have stopped arguing.\
Something on the instrumentation can become impossible in a very small way. A reading arrives that corresponds to a control change Johnny hasn't made. Then another. Or the rail reports a harness position it is only moving towards.\
And somewhere in there Johnny reaches the speed he has been pursuing\'97or the apparatus effectively drives itself into the equivalent state despite him trying to back away.\
Then the universe ends.\
And:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \strokec3 That was when Sarah's waters broke.
\f0\b0 \strokec3 \
I think that works best if it is literally the final narrative fact. The machine's catastrophe does not need to be narrated after it. The book has spent an enormous amount of effort on universes, causality, Little Clinton, pregnancy and the One After the One. Ending the old universe at the exact physical beginning of birth gives you the collision without explaining it.\
For Aeon, therefore, I would make the 
\f1\b Johnny\'96Chip showdown immediately precede Sarah's waters breaking
\f0\b0 , and let its calendar placement resolve from whatever fixed constraint you ultimately retain for Little Clinton's birth. The Project Kebab events leading into it can remain relative for now.\
}